Well, the farthest I've ever taken a Tourist is level 4, where he discovered
how ineffective +2 darts were against a swarm of killer bees...  "Kill,
Rover, kill!!!"  I find the best strategy is to stay on the 1st level until
you reach 4th level (make any sense?), and feed all the corpses to your
dog/cat, as you start off with a plethora of food.  By then, both you
and your pet will be strong enough to take on 2nd-level monsters, and
hopefully you'll have picked up a bit of armor, like a hat.  On level 2,
wait around for a dwarf to kill, since he could carry armor, a shield,
boots, and possibly a magic cloak.  You know how to identify cursed items
without the use of altars, don't you?  All old hack players should know...

